    "title": "2 men in critical condition after Christmas Eve shooting in Winston-Salem - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Justyn Araya DeBusk ,\n59 minutes ago\nWINSTON-SALEM, N.C. (WGHP) — Two people are in critical condition after a shooting on Christmas Eve in Winston-Salem.\nAt about 9:35 p.m. on Wednesday, police responded to a shooting on the 2900 block of New Walkertown Road in Winston-Salem.\nAt the scene, officers found Keivaunaugh Cearon Sanders, 24, and Fernando Monta Noel, 46, suffering from gunshot wounds. They were both taken to a hospital in critical condition.\nPolice did not release any information regarding possible motives or suspects but did note that this appears to be an isolated incident.\nAnyone with information is asked to call the WSPD at (336) 773-7700, Crime Stoppers at (336) 727-2800 or En Espanol (336) 728-3904. Tips made to Crime Stoppers can be made anonymously. A Crime Stoppers Tip Form can also be located online . You can also view “ Crime Stoppers of Winston-Salem Forsyth County ” on Facebook. Tips, including photos and videos, can be texted to the WSPD at (336) 276-1717. Text tips are not anonymous.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX8 WGHP.",
